Links 2.30 for PsiWeb: memory (PsiWeb 1.00, the memory review of November 2026). Applied by
links/fetch.sh after links-2.30-psion.diff, links-2.30-scrollbar.diff and links-2.30-style.diff.
- cache.c (PSIWEB): psi_cache_free_decompressed: Trim drops the inflated copy of every page
- compress.c (PSIWEB): a compressed page is inflated no further than PSI_HEAP_STOP short of the
  engine's room: what came is shown and the page says it was cut (psi_page_cut); the block starts
  at the length the page had last time, or four times the compressed length
- cookies.c (PSIWEB): cookies written out only when one changed (psi_cookies_changed); at most
  300 kept, 30 for a domain, the oldest going first
- html_r.c, html_tbl.c (PSIWEB): the colour lookup at 256 heads; the table cache at 1,024 heads
  with no initialiser (32 KB of zeros out of the program's data)
- img.c, links.h (PSI_LAZY_IMAGES): psi_drop_other_pages: when a page is done, the finished
  pictures of other pages (the page before, kept for Back) go
- jpeg.c (PSI_LAZY_IMAGES): a progressive JPEG asked only for its size is not started (libjpeg
  allocated every coefficient of the whole picture for it); for a real decode the coefficients
  are counted first, and a picture whose arrays would not fit is refused
  (PSI_PIC_MAX_BYTES on the 5mx, twice it on the netBook)
- links.h, compress.c, cache.c (PSIWEB): psi_last_dlen, a page's inflated length last time
- session.c (PSIWEB): psi_history_cap: the Back list cut to a length when a page is done

